## Lore

Most people know the Headhunter Assassin by another name: the Brutal Killer,
or B.K. Where other Headhunters hire out as soldiers, guards or trackers, this
one sells a single service. A B.K. finds a named target and ends it. Capture
jobs are turned down, and so are theft, recovery work and frame-ups; a client
who wants anything other than a death is told, bluntly, to hire someone else.

The work is done coldly and to the letter of the contract. The killer accepts
only loose limits on method, takes no side jobs, and does not rob the body
afterwards, because the fee is the whole of the payment. Anyone standing
between the Assassin and the target is an obstacle to be removed, and deadly
force is the usual tool, though an opponent who is down and no longer a threat
is simply ignored. Bystanders may get a few curt words of warning. When the
target is dead the Assassin leaves at once, without revenge or lingering.

Brutal Killers hide their faces and names. The dark, unreflective armor, often
with a skull or demon faceplate, comes out only for meeting a client and for
the hunt; the rest of the time they pass as ordinary mercenaries. They are rare
among Headhunters, almost always evil, hard to bribe or frighten, and those who
pretend to be one of them seldom get away with it for long.

## GM Notes

Called shots: +1 to strike on a called shot at levels 2, 5 and 11, added by
hand. The stored +2 to disarm is printed as applying in hand to hand combat or
on a Called Shot.

Military skills taken as O.C.C. Related picks get +5% only on Demolitions and
the Trap skills.

Find Contraband is the narrow Headhunter form: arms dealers, bionics and
weapons smugglers, chop-shops and underground Cyber-Docs, not drugs or magic.

Starting kit beyond what the sheet lists: one heavy energy rifle and one
sidearm of choice (six E-Clips each), three more weapons of the player''s choosing,
each with three magazines, and personal items. The backpack may instead be an NG-S2
survival pack. Armor is typically matte black or another dark color with no
reflective surfaces: one light suit for espionage work and one heavy suit for
combat.

Transportation can be almost anything but leans to small, fast vehicles such
as hovercycles; power armor is used by some, Techno-Wizard gear by a few, and
a small share ride M.D.C. animals.

Money: besides the credits, 3D4x1000 credits in black market salable items.

Cybernetics: 1D4 implants of choice, plus one bionic limb with two bionic
weapons or features.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'headhunter-assassin');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
-- these, and a CR in the stored markdown means the checkout mangled the file.
SELECT class_id, name, status, length(markdown) AS bytes, instr(markdown, char(13)) > 0 AS has_cr
  FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'headhunter-assassin';

-- Records this run. REQUIRED: the smoke test fails a data script that has no
-- footer, or whose footer names a different file.
INSERT INTO data_script_runs (filename) VALUES ('add-headhunter-assassin-class.sql');
